  "Number": 4,
  "Question": "Estimate to determine which of the following is closest to\n\n\\[\\frac{401}{0.205}.\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0.2\\)",
    "B": "\\(2\\)",
    "C": "\\(20\\)",
    "D": "\\(200\\)",
    "E": "\\(2000\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The numerator is close to \\(400\\), and the denominator is close to \\(0.2\\). These convenient numbers give\n\\[\n\\frac{401}{0.205}\\approx\\frac{400}{0.2}\n=\\frac{4000}{2}=2000.\n\\]\nWe can confirm that this estimate selects the closest choice without finding the exact quotient:\n\\[\n0.205\\cdot1900=389.5<401<410=0.205\\cdot2000.\n\\]\nBecause the divisor \\(0.205\\) is positive, the quotient lies between \\(1900\\) and \\(2000\\). Its distance from \\(2000\\) is less than \\(100\\). Every other choice is at most \\(200\\), so its distance from the quotient is greater than \\(1700\\). Thus the closest value is \\(2000\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
